{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1453830-npcs-abusing-pc-quiet","id":1453830,"title":"NPCs abusing PC Quiet?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-06-30T03:51:23-07:00","id":1453830,"title":"NPCs abusing PC Quiet?","content":"I just had an idea for a story-driven warning to players with regards to treating hobgoblins as if they weren't real. It's perfectly reasonable that a wilful mage could deny her delusions and force herself not to interact with them, and given that it comes with a cost in Willpower and some difficult rolls, it's not unfair.<br /> <br /> That said, I imagine there would be Mages of all stripes, and some non-Mages, who would be prepared to take full advantage of this refusal to interact. Picture a reality hacker showing up in a clown costume to rifle through the Mage's possessions, photograph her ongoing work, feed her misinformation (or misleading ideas). Or a necromancer sending their ghosts to interfere with the Mage's work and life, knowing that they will be mistaken for expressions of her madness.<br /> <br /> Even if these efforts have mixed successes, they are horrible for the Mage and for the player; a whole new layer of paranoia over what is real enters play. Is this a real thing deliberately intended to look fake, or a fake thing that seems incredibly real? Where am I, what am I doing, am I being watched? If the overall goal is driving the Mage so mad that they are lost forever, such provocations are quite likely to succeed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-30T10:52:29-07:00","id":1453851,"title":"","content":"I think you need too much player buy-in to really make this idea fun at the table without ruining the emotional impact desired.<br /> <br /> Also, from a practical in-universe standpoint, who would bother actually getting good at this? Mages undergoing a Quiet don't have a big sign around their neck saying so. They also likely still have friends and allies looking out for them. I can fully get behind the idea that lots of people in the setting would be willing to take advantage of this, but the lack of opportunity makes the idea of being prepared to do so dubious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-30T15:20:46-07:00","id":1453870,"title":"","content":"It would take some Mind and/or Entropy to determine what hobgoblins the PC Mage is seeing. This subplot would work really well in a one on one campaign. In a group of players, the infiltrator's disguise is only effective against one member of the Cabal. The Cabal has to be together most of the time for the session to roll. The spy will be spotted fast enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-01T01:05:00-07:00","id":1453899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1453830-npcs-abusing-pc-quiet?p=1453870#post1453870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It would take some Mind and/or Entropy to determine what hobgoblins the PC Mage is seeing. This subplot would work really well in a one on one campaign. In a group of players, the infiltrator's disguise is only effective against one member of the Cabal. The Cabal has to be together most of the time for the session to roll. The spy will be spotted fast enough.</div> </div> </div> </div>As Quiet reaches level 4, Hobgoblins become visible to people other than the Mage. Furthermore, Mages don't know how extreme another Mage's Quiet is - if you know another Mage is losing it, and there's a guy in a pink elephant mascot costume playing a flute in their room, the idea that it's a manifestation of their madness or a demented application of their Magick would at least cross your mind.<br /> <br /> That said, yes, simply showing up and walking around in the open with a Mage who is only slightly compromised would be a bad idea, since you'd stick out. We're talking a serious Quiet issue, the kind which would have entered the rumour mill as people worry about what will happen if it doesn't resolve. Mages do like to keep an eye on one another, it's part of the reason Sects exist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 07-01-2021, 04:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-01T01:08:36-07:00","id":1453900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1453830-npcs-abusing-pc-quiet?p=1453851#post1453851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you need too much player buy-in to really make this idea fun at the table without ruining the emotional impact desired.<br /> <br /> Also, from a practical in-universe standpoint, who would bother actually getting good at this? Mages undergoing a Quiet don't have a big sign around their neck saying so. They also likely still have friends and allies looking out for them. I can fully get behind the idea that lots of people in the setting would be willing to take advantage of this, but the lack of opportunity makes the idea of being prepared to do so dubious.</div> </div> </div> </div>The opportunity relates to a rumour mill around Mages who are losing their touch with reality - in the Traditions for instance, part of the point of Mages of different groups interacting is to keep an eye out for emerging Marauders. Witches live in covens of three for a reason. One is a tragedy, two is an argument, three is a coven. It's a very, very niche way of messing with someone, and it's also extremely cruel, so the number of people who would be:<br /> <br /> - informed<br /> - equipped<br /> - willing<br /> <br /> Would be a short list. That said, Mages are all about doing the impossible, and if you have an opportunity to rob your greatest rival blind and drive them even more mad in the process... of course any Mage with a conscience or a fear of the damage a true Marauder might do would think twice, but both MTA and the real world hold plenty of examples of people performing selfish acts for short term gain.<br /> <br /> This is all assuming the Hobgoblin Impersonator doesn't bother to use their own magick - projecting a mental illusion that only the target can see, worsening their delusions, showing up in person when they're alone or once their madness has become bad enough that a nearby Mage would buy it manifesting in reality... the possibilities are endless.<br /> <br /> Finally, M20 does hold references to people deliberately driving a Mage mad. The writeup for Denial Quiet mentions how Nephandi love to sow the seeds for them, since it allows them to operate more easily. Basically we've got prior for Mages abusing the madness of others... one which illustrates how committed and evil you need to be of course.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 07-01-2021, 04:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-01T04:08:18-07:00","id":1453911,"title":"","content":"And.... why would a player want to play with a ST that uses their power over what sorts of backlashes happen to force a Quiet into the game just to have a NPC purposefully built to screw over characters in Quiet? How do you keep the player engaged with the paranoia instead of them just rage quitting because you're trolling them, at best?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-01T06:47:20-07:00","id":1453927,"title":"","content":"I think it's an interesting idea, but (as said) could also be problematic. There's a danger to fall into an &quot;I got you!&quot; that's fun for the ST but rarely for the players. Like: Making invisible enemies when you know the players never bother to detect illusions, or making enemies with oracular powers predict the plans of the players because you know the players never bothered to place a time ward...etc.<br /> <br /> These possibilities are firmly part of the setting, but even then it's tricky...it's the kind of things that can cause &quot;rage quits&quot; if done wrong. That's why many ST's use the tools of the game to give clues about what the players migth not be thinking about, but the characters (being Mages that know how Mages &amp; magick opperate) might suspect or think about.<br /> <br /> In Vampire there was a Merit that covered some of these situations, &quot;Common Sense&quot; or something like that if I'm not mistaken. That the capability of being given a warning before you screw up (as <i>player </i>that may not know a few things that the ST knows and your PC migth know) it's a Merit talks about how much Vampire was liable to screw with the players this way. It was said to be ideal for newbies in my RPG circle - nowdays I think it should be free<br /> <br /> If enemies posing as Hobgoblins it's something that &quot;happens&quot; in the setting (I guess it could, depending on how Quiets and Hobgoblins are treated), then it's something the characters should know about - even if they're green, they're supposedly initiated and had/have mentors and other superiors that teach and give advice (this aid it's one of the main reasons to join and remain into a Sect). Players need to share this knowledge to better build their agency","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-01T15:08:18-07:00","id":1453976,"title":"","content":"If the hobgoblin has begun to have a kind of independent existence, it is going to take offense at the Mage impersonating it. I have an idea of how you might do it. Write some personality characteristics for this hobgoblin. Have it do and say things in between discussion of other parts of the story. If the afflicted character or Cabal takes no interest in those details, then they are going to have no basis of comparison between two different hobgoblins. <br /> <br /> There is another idea. What if you reversed it? Create a powerful enemy NPC Mage who would be hard to defeat by &quot;normal&quot; means. Some contact or Chantry Intelligence Agent informs the the players that he has a nasty hobgoblin. The players have to study the time intervals between this thing's manifestations to know when it is likely to be absent so they can project their way into a Technomancer Sanctum.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-05T09:36:49-07:00","id":1454282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And.... why would a player want to play with a ST that uses their power over what sorts of backlashes happen to force a Quiet into the game just to have a NPC purposefully built to screw over characters in Quiet? </div> </div> </div>Ah damn, I've been figured out by this good faith response, this is definitely a thing that I said STs should do. And I would have gotten away with it if not for these meddling forum users!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-05T09:39:44-07:00","id":1454283,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar26467_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26467\" data-vbnamecard=\"26467\">HorizonParty2021</a> very good point with the Hobgoblin itself interfering with impersonation! This is particularly interesting because it's possible that a Mage who sees two &quot;delusions&quot; arguing and fighting one another might:<br /> <br /> - realize something has gone wrong<br /> - think they're going EXTRA insane and seek help<br /> <br /> Either way it won't work out well for the impersonator, who might wind up going mad themselves as a kind of karmic justice for trying to exploit another Mage's quiet.<br /> <br /> As for the PCs being asked to do it to an NPC, that also works well as a plot hook, good idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-05T09:42:03-07:00","id":1454284,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1683_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1683\" data-vbnamecard=\"1683\">Aleph</a> yeah even something as simple as Mages talking about how insanity is incredibly tricky when you deal with reality-warping powers. For example, a tale about a Mage who presumes the Bygone crawling through their sanctum is just their imagination, and winds up being torn to shreds by a Manticore. This isn't a direct warning from the ST to watch out for &quot;fake Hobgoblins&quot;, but it at least makes sure that the players and player characters are aware, in principle, that sometimes it's very dangerous to chalk something up to madness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}